activate-credential-sequence-object: TPM2_ActivateCredential rejects a sequence object as activateHandle

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, "TPM2_ActivateCredential", "General
Description"): "This command enables the association of a credential with an
object in a way that ensures that the TPM has validated the parameters of the
credentialed object."

A hash, HMAC or event sequence object has no parameters the TPM validated,
yet the reference activates a credential for it, using whatever Name an
earlier object left in the slot. The specification gives no response code for
this case; the check returns TPM_RC_TYPE + RC_ActivateCredential_activateHandle
after the keyHandle checks, as the TCG reference's version 185 ("Cannot
activate credential of sequence object") and tpm-rs do.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Object/ActivateCredential.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Object/ActivateCredential.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Object/ActivateCredential.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Object/ActivateCredential.c
@@ -43,6 +43,12 @@
        || !IS_ATTRIBUTE(object->publicArea.objectAttributes, TPMA_OBJECT, restricted))
         return TPM_RCS_TYPE + RC_ActivateCredential_keyHandle;
 
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // a sequence object has no validated parameters to associate a credential
+    // with (as in version 185: "Cannot activate credential of sequence object").
+    if(ObjectIsSequence(activateObject))
+        return TPM_RCS_TYPE + RC_ActivateCredential_activateHandle;
+
     // Command output
 
     // Decrypt input credential data via asymmetric decryption.  A
